From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mempage4k <mempage4k@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wgpu-hal: Vulkan depthBiasClamp enabled where advertised

The adapter reports DownlevelFlags::DEPTH_BIAS_CLAMP when the device
supports depthBiasClamp, but the device was created without the feature,
so a depth bias with a clamp (static, or set_depth_bias of 0002) was
outside what the device enabled: the validation layers report
VUID-vkCmdSetDepthBias-depthBiasClamp-00790 for every shadow draw of a
game on a Pixel 8a. The feature is now enabled with the flag.
---
diff --git a/src/vulkan/adapter.rs b/src/vulkan/adapter.rs
index 606fcee..5a050a4 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/adapter.rs
+++ b/src/vulkan/adapter.rs
@@ -318,6 +318,9 @@ impl PhysicalDeviceFeatures {
                 .sampler_anisotropy(
                     downlevel_flags.contains(wgt::DownlevelFlags::ANISOTROPIC_FILTERING),
                 )
+                // Advertised as DEPTH_BIAS_CLAMP when the device has it
+                // (`set_depth_bias` passes the clamp): enabled with it.
+                .depth_bias_clamp(downlevel_flags.contains(wgt::DownlevelFlags::DEPTH_BIAS_CLAMP))
                 .texture_compression_etc2(
                     requested_features.contains(wgt::Features::TEXTURE_COMPRESSION_ETC2),
                 )
